ops there we go something like  that could work quite well as well or I  actually like Titans color scheme quite  a bit too which is yellow with black  which turns out quite interesting it's  actually a bit more gold in this case I  might want to make that a little bit  lighter there's just many ways to have  some variety in these color schemes but  what I would want to say is that usually  the the real-life ones don't have to  interesting or too bright color schemes  not like many modern benhams would have  they are quite boring and predictable  color schemes in a sense anyway that  just about rounds it up for this video  about arrow hyper coasters it's not  really the best one ever but it's really  just a general idea of how you can make  one of these and I wanted to close this  video with another look at how we could  look in a real-life setting you really  do want to bring out the skyline of  these things as much as you can like  wherever they are placed they were  really placed in such a way that you can  see them and be like whoa that is really  one heck of a tall coaster since they  really were some record breakers back in  the day nowadays they're sort of  neglected and nobody at Cedar Point  really goes to magnum XL 200 anymore  well some people definitely do but  they're not really the most popular  rides anymore and they're overshadowed  by many courses that have been built in  much more recent years but there's still  a very classic staple of rollercoasters  despite only a few being builds and  there are still many kinds of very  modern hybrids being built which are  still sort of legacy of the old Aero  Hyper's which I'll talk about in some  later videos but this is really all I  have to say about this one so I hope you  guys enjoyed this video and learn  something from it and if you have any  feedback or questions don't be afraid to  leave it in the comment section below  and I'll see you guys in the next video
 

